# Git authorship and rewrite safety

## Author identity (required)

Commits for this IcedTea-Web repo must use:

- **Name:** `Martin Hickson`
- **Email:** `martinhickson@users.noreply.github.com`

Do **not** use `mhickson@bravurasolutions.com` as the git author/committer for commits pushed to GitHub.

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — match recent history on the repo
git -c user.name="Martin Hickson" -c user.email="martinhickson@users.noreply.github.com" commit ...
```

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git commit  # if local user.email is bravurasolutions.com
# Author: Martin Hickson <mhickson@bravurasolutions.com>
```

## No Cursor / CursorAgent co-author

Never add these trailers (or any Cursor agent co-author):

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `Co-authored-by: CursorAgent ...`

Strip them if a hook or UI inserted them before amending/rebasing.

## Before every push — check

Run and confirm clean authorship on commits being pushed:

```bash
git log origin/<branch>..HEAD --format='Author: %an <%ae>%n%b'
# or, if no upstream yet:
git log -3 --format='Author: %an <%ae>%n%s%n%b'
```

Push only if:

1. Author/committer email is `martinhickson@users.noreply.github.com`
2. No `Co-authored-by: Cursor` / `cursoragent` lines appear in the bodies

## Before every rebase (or history rewrite) — backup pointer

**Always** copy the current branch tip first with `git branch -c` (does not switch branches):

```bash
git branch -c "<current-branch>-backup-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
# example: feature/sqlite-cache-catalog-backup-20260813-072800
```

Then rebase / filter / reset. Keep the backup branch until the rewrite is verified and pushed.
